<title>ITALY: Specialists bid for 293 bln lire of Italy CTZ.</title>
<headline>Specialists bid for 293 bln lire of Italy CTZ.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Specialist bond traders bid for 293 billion lire of zero coupon, two-year Treasury certificates (CTZ) against the Italian Treasury's offer of 250 billion lire of paper.</p>
<p>Earlier, the Treasury received bids for 6.468 trillion lire at the open auction for the August 31, 1998 paper, against 2.5 trillion lire worth of certificates on offer.</p>
<p>The auction price was set at 86.00 from 85.35 at the previous CTZ sale on August 26, with a gross yield of 7.99 percent against 8.23 percent.</p>
</text>
